Gooo browser body-codegen adapter

The compiler is the unmodified MIT-licensed Gooo compiler at revision
90ff2bb5aeffc2ac553496b646d14db1e8d33fdb. Its source-assembly dispatch is adapted
in bridge/adapter.go.txt with the original copyright and MIT terms preserved.
The compiler and copied compiler fixtures retain the MIT license in
LICENSE-COMPILER (Copyright 2026 Kim Joo-yoon). The separate browser bridge
is distributed under these same MIT terms.

The linked gooo-decision-runtime v0.2.41-experimental uses the MIT license in
LICENSE-DECISION-RUNTIME (Copyright 2026 Gooo contributors).
The Go standard library and wasm_exec.js use the BSD license preserved in
../../third_party/GO-LICENSE.

Other locally authored fixture probes and browser page assets use the repository's
BSD license in ../../LICENSE. Fixture origins, immutable revisions, raw source
hashes and source-file paths are recorded in fixtures.json.

Prepared with OpenAI Codex assistance. Independent of Google and the Go project.
The page generates Go through the actual compiler library; it does not execute
the generated Go or expose the full CLI, package imports or model/provider files.
The separate bridge provenance does not replace UNBOUND_LOCAL_SOURCE in the
compiler's own build report.
